<title>UK: India 1996 wheat exports at 1.5 mln T - official.</title>
<headline>India 1996 wheat exports at 1.5 mln T - official.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's wheat exports will total 1.5 million tonnes in 1996, a senior government official said during a visit to London.</p>
<p>S.P. Jakhanwal, government secretary in charge of food procurement and distribution at the Ministry of Food, said India had completed wheat exports for this year and had no more to sell. But rice exports were continuing.</p>
<p>He was speaking to Reuters after attending the International Grains Council (IGC) session on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The IGC has estimated India's wheat exports in the 1996/97 (July/June) crop season at 600,000 tonnes from 1.5 million tonnes in 1995/96.</p>
<p>-- Clelia Oziel, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8072</p>
